  "coaching": {
    "summary": "The decision sits at the intersection of two compounding problems — a reliability deficit that suppresses sales effectiveness and rising engineering attrition that worsens that deficit — making the causal chain from hiring choice to ARR growth non-trivial to trace. Strengthening the reasoning means surfacing missing links, testing the Q3 timeline assumption, and guarding against the framing that more sellers automatically means more revenue.",
    "strengthen_items": [
      {
        "id": "link-reliability-to-quota",
        "label": "Make the reliability-to-quota-attainment link explicit",
        "detail": "The brief states the sales team 'already misses quota with the current product reliability,' yet the causal structure does not connect Platform Reliability Improvement back to Current Sales Quota Attainment — closing this loop would reveal whether fixing reliability is a prerequisite for any sales headcount to be effective.",
        "action_type": "add_risk",
        "bias_category": "narrow_framing"
      },
      {
        "id": "add-time-lag-constraint",
        "label": "Introduce a time-to-impact constraint for the Q3 deadline",
        "detail": "Neither engineering ramp-up time nor sales ramp-to-productivity is represented, yet both affect whether any option can plausibly move New ARR Generated or Platform Reliability Improvement before the board's Q3 milestone.",
        "action_type": "add_constraint",
        "bias_category": "overconfidence"
      },
      {
        "id": "link-attrition-to-reliability-loop",
        "label": "Capture the attrition-reliability feedback loop",
